    "interpretation": "**Minto** is the mechanistic baseline, fitted on this very cohort. It explains 94.1% of the variance (R\u00b2 0.941), with RMSE 7.85 and MAE 4.11 ng/mL. Residual dispersion falls from 16.5x across concentration terciles on the natural scale to 2.0x in log space, which is the empirical case for the multiplicative grey-box form. Log residuals are near-symmetric (skew +0.37) but heavy-tailed (kurtosis 4.48 vs 3.0 for a normal), so Gaussian prediction intervals would be mis-calibrated - hence the distribution-free conformal intervals. Durbin-Watson of 0.33 (against 2.0 for independence) and an intraclass correlation of 0.36 confirm strong within-patient dependence, which is why splitting and bootstrapping are both done at subject level."
  },
