    "caveat": "Axes min\u2013max scaled across candidate models. Area is not a quality score.",
    "caveat_detail": "Each axis is independently min\u2013max normalised across the nine candidate models, so a polygon shows relative position on each axis, not absolute merit. The axes are not commensurable, so polygon area carries no meaning and models must not be ranked by it. Two axes in particular reward uniform error rather than good error: Homoscedasticity and Normality (AD*). The pure-ML ablation scores at the top of both because its residuals are uniformly poor across the concentration range, not because it is a better model. Read R\u00b2, RMSE, MDPE and PI coverage as performance; read Homoscedasticity and Normality as assumption checks."
